message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Generic VarVAMP qPCR Workflow"

type: software

authors:

* family-names: "Faham"
  given-names: "Ayman"

version: 1.1.0

date-released: 2026-07-25

license: GPL-3.0-or-later

repository-code: "https://github.com/Epigenome-Sb/varVAMP-qPCR-workflow"

url: "https://github.com/Epigenome-Sb/varVAMP-qPCR-workflow"

abstract: >-
An interactive and reproducible command-line workflow for nucleotide
sequence dereplication, multiple sequence alignment, conservation analysis,
and qPCR primer/probe design using CD-HIT-EST, MAFFT, and VarVAMP.
The workflow provides explicit scientific parameter checkpoints for
CD-HIT-EST clustering, MAFFT alignment strategy selection, and VarVAMP
qPCR design parameters.

keywords:

* qPCR
* primer design
* probe design
* VarVAMP
* CD-HIT-EST
* MAFFT
* multiple sequence alignment
* sequence dereplication
* conservation analysis
* nucleotide sequences
* bioinformatics
* reproducible workflow
